    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Founded by Roger II in 1130, it joined <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#sicily">Sicily</a> and southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#italy">Italy</a> in one of medieval <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#europe">Europe</a>’s most centralised states.</li><li>Its Norman court mixed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#latin">Latin</a>, Greek and Arabic government and art, seen in Palermo, Cefalù and Monreale.</li><li>After the Vespers of 1282 it survived as an island kingdom under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#kingdom-of-aragon">Aragon</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#spain">Spain</a> and others until 1816.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>From 1530 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#knights-hospitaller">Knights Hospitaller</a> held Malta as a fief of the kingdom, paying the king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#sicily">Sicily</a> an annual tribute of a single falcon.</p></aside>
    </section>

